{"id":"admah","name":"Admah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:admah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Admah","text":"Earth, one of the five cities of the vale of Siddim (Gen. 10:19). It was destroyed along with Sodom and Gomorrah (19:24; Deut. 29:23). It is supposed by some to be the same as the Adam of Josh. 3:16, the name of which still lingers in Damieh, the ford of Jordan. (See ZEBOIM.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H126","lemma":"אַדְמָה","xlit":"ʼAdmâh","gloss":"Admah, a place near the Dead Sea","kjv":"Admah","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H6636","lemma":"צְבֹאִים","xlit":"Tsᵉbôʼîym","gloss":"Tseboim or Tsebijim, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Zeboiim, Zeboim","count":4,"share":1},{"strong":"H6017","lemma":"עֲמֹרָה","xlit":"ʻĂmôrâh","gloss":"Amorah, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Gomorrah","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H5467","lemma":"סְדֹם","xlit":"Çᵉdôm","gloss":"Sedom, a place near the Dead Sea","kjv":"Sodom","count":3,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H2015","lemma":"הָפַךְ","xlit":"hâphak","gloss":"to turn about or over","kjv":"become, change, come, be converted","count":2,"share":0.5}],"verses":["Gen.10.19","Gen.14.2","Deut.29.23","Hos.11.8"],"related":[{"id":"zeboim","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.571,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"gomorrah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.103,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"sodom","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.033,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"zeboim","type":"lexical","strong":"H126","why":"both lead with אַדְמָה (H126)"}],"works":[{"work":"anf02","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 2: Fathers of the Second Century","count":2,"chapters":[{"chapter":"ANFVI.2","count":2,"book":"Theophilus to Autolycus","title":"Book II"}]}]}
